{"term":"perennial","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:caef5760ab3b4fdd15","definition":"Lasting or remaining active throughout the year, for multiple years, or all the time.","example":"a perennial stream","pos":"adj","synonyms":["multiyear","yearslong","perennal"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonperennial","perennialism","perennialist","perenniality","perennialization","perennialize","perennially","perennialness","perennial philosophy","perenniation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perennial#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e6f63e7d5521e14232","definition":"Continuing without cessation or intermission for several years, or for an undetermined or infinite period; never-ending or never failing; perpetual, unceasing.","example":"His artwork has a perennial beauty.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["continual","enduring","everlasting","permanent","timeless","ageful","agelong","amaranthine","celestial","endless","enduring","eternal","eterne","everduring","evergreen","everlasting","eviternal","forever","heavenly","imperishable","indesinent","lasting","never-ending","perennial","permanent","perpetual","perpetuate","persistent","sempiternal","timeless","unending","undeadly","undying"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, not-comparable","register":"figuratively, not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonperennial","perennialism","perennialist","perenniality","perennialization","perennialize","perennially","perennialness","perennial philosophy","perenniation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perennial#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:44aa3de33fb719e268","definition":"Appearing or recurring again and again; recurrent.","example":"a perennial candidate in elections","pos":"adj","synonyms":["repetitious","habitual","monotonous","perennial","recurrent","recurring","repeating","repetitional","repetitionary","repetitious","repetitive"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, not-comparable","register":"figuratively, not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonperennial","perennialism","perennialist","perenniality","perennialization","perennialize","perennially","perennialness","perennial philosophy","perenniation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perennial#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:86bd308c18972c0103","definition":"Of a plant: active throughout the year, or having a life cycle of more than two growing seasons.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonperennial","perennialism","perennialist","perenniality","perennialization","perennialize","perennially","perennialness","perennial philosophy","perenniation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perennial#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:31ff46fd7e50fee103","definition":"A plant that is active throughout the year, or has a life cycle of more than two growing seasons.","example":"One would have supposed from the appearance of the country at the end of the first season after the eruption that practically all plants except the trees and bushes had been destroyed, and that revegetation must be due to new seedlings started on the ash. Such, however, is not the case. Excavation of the root systems of the new plants shows that they are old perennials which have come through the ash from the old soil.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["nonperennial","perennialism","perennialist","perenniality",